# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# www -> apex, 301. Both hostnames are attached to the Pages project, so
# without this Cloudflare serves byte-identical content on both and the
# ranking signal splits between two addresses (Roadmap 2.6.1).
#
# This lives in the build rather than as a zone Redirect Rule on purpose: it is
# version-controlled, it travels with the repo, and it cannot silently drift
# from a dashboard setting nobody remembers changing.
#
# The `!` forces the redirect even though a matching static file exists.
# :splat carries the rest of the path through, so deep links survive.
https://www.edventures.pet/* https://edventures.pet/:splat 301!
